abstract:
The most elegant idea in classical machine learning. Data that no line can separate becomes separable in a higher-dimensional space — but you never have to visit that space. Because the SVM dual touches the data only through inner products, replacing $\langle x_i,x_j\rangle$ with a kernel $K(x_i,x_j)$ silently performs the lift. We verify the trick numerically, derive the polynomial expansion, show the RBF kernel corresponds to infinite dimensions, and map out how $\gamma$ and $C$ interact.}
